# Expense Service Development Rules (Python/FastAPI)

## Import Conventions
- Use absolute imports: `from app.models.expense import Expense`
- Avoid relative imports within the `app` package

## Multi-tenancy
- Every database query MUST be scoped by `tenant_id`
- Check `tenant.llm_monthly_used < tenant.llm_monthly_budget` before LLM API calls
- All API endpoints must respect tenant isolation

## API Routes
- All routes must use `/api/v1/...` prefix
- Use `async def` for all API endpoints
- Response models must be Pydantic v2 `BaseModel`

## Linting & Formatting
- Run from `expense-service/`: `uv run ruff check .` before commits
- Run from `expense-service/`: `uv run ruff format .` to format
- Fix all Ruff issues before claiming work complete

## Testing
- Run from `expense-service/`: `uv run python -m pytest tests/ -v --tb=short`
- SQLite used for in-memory unit tests
- PostgreSQL-specific features have SQLite compile-time stubs

## Docstrings
- Preserve all existing docstrings and comments
- Do not remove comments unless explicitly asked

## Shared Contracts
- Reuse Pydantic DTOs and transport-safe enums from `common/python/expense-contracts`
- Keep SQLAlchemy models, migrations, and database metadata inside `expense-service`
